  "pr_title": "build(tooling): add a Nuitka standalone build of the CLI",
  "pr_description": "## Goal\n\nBuild the spsync command-line tool as a standalone macOS folder that runs without Python or uv. The Obsidian plugin can then download one archive instead of asking teammates to install Python tooling.\n\n## Summary\n\n`scripts/build_standalone.sh` compiles the CLI with Nuitka in standalone mode. It builds for the architecture of the Mac that runs it and writes `dist/spsync-macos-<arch>.tar.gz`. The archive holds one folder with the `spsync` executable and its libraries. The script installs the locked runtime dependencies and Nuitka into its own environment under `build/`, so the project `.venv` stays unchanged.\n\nThe prototype compared PyInstaller one-file and one-folder, Nuitka standalone and one-file, and PyApp on arm64 and x86_64. Nuitka standalone had the fastest start, at about 136 ms for `--help` on arm64, which matters because automatic sync runs the CLI often. The issue comment on #15 records the size, start time, test, Gatekeeper, Automation, and Keychain results.\n\n`pyproject.toml` adds a `build` dependency group with Nuitka. It also constrains cryptography to versions below 49 on Intel Macs, because cryptography 49 and later publish no Intel macOS wheels. The lockfile now has cryptography 48.0.1 for Intel Macs and 50.0.2 elsewhere. The README describes the build.\n\nThe archive bundles merge3, which is licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later. The license terms for distributing the archive are an open question for the release workflow (#11). The issue comment on #15 records that question.\n\nThe change does not touch docx reading or patching.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `uv run ruff format --check`, `uv run ruff check`, `uv run ty check`, `uv run anti-slop-python src tests`, and `uv run pytest` pass.\n- `scripts/build_standalone.sh` built `dist/spsync-macos-arm64.tar.gz`. Obsidian downloaded the archive with `requestUrl` and unpacked it. The build then passed `pull`, `push`, and `sync` with the local backend and the Word backend, with no Python, uv, or Node on `PATH`.\n- Manual check still needed: run the arm64 build on a Mac without the Xcode Command Line Tools, and build and run the x86_64 archive on an Intel Mac.\n\n## Issue\n\nRefs #15\n"
